<h2>COSMAC VIP</h2>

<p><strong>32K.xml</strong></p>
<p>
COSMAC VIP with 32K RAM, using the patched <code>vip.32.rom</code> file.
</p>

<p><strong>chip8.xml</strong></p>
<p>
COSMAC VIP running Chip-8, using the patched <code>vip.32.rom</code> file.
</p>

<p>
Select a Chip-8 file in the <strong>RAM</strong> field or use <code>LOAD</code> after <strong>Start</strong>.
</p>

<p><strong>chip8x-vp580-vp590-vp595.xml</strong></p>
<p>
COSMAC VIP running Chip-8X with VP580, VP590 and VP595 expansion boards, using the patched <code>vip.32.rom</code> file. Select a Chip-8 file in the RAM field or use <code>LOAD</code> after <code>Start</code>.
</p>

<p><strong>chip10.xml</strong></p>
<p>
COSMAC VIP running Chip-10, using the patched <code>vip.32.rom</code> file. Select a Chip-8 file in the RAM field or use <code>LOAD</code> after <code>Start</code>.
</p>

<p><strong>fpb-vp590.xml</strong></p>
<p>
COSMAC VIP running Fixed Point Basic with the VP590 board, using the patched <code>vip.32.rom</code> file.
</p>

<p><strong>fpb.xml</strong></p>
<p>
COSMAC VIP running Fixed Point Basic, using the patched <code>vip.32.rom</code> file.
</p>

<p><strong>pin-8-vp550-&lt;stereo&gt;.xml</strong></p>
<p>
COSMAC VIP running Pin8 with a VP550 board in mono or stereo.
</p>

<p><strong>pin-8-vp551-&lt;stereo&gt;.xml</strong></p>
<p>
COSMAC VIP running Pin8 with a VP551 board in mono or stereo.
</p>

<p><strong>superchip-vp590-vp595.xml</strong></p>
<p>
Custom VIP SuperChip interpreter running with VP590 and VP595 boards.
</p>

<p><strong>vp550.xml</strong></p>
<p>
COSMAC VIP running with a VP550 board.
</p>

<p><strong>vp551.xml</strong></p>
<p>
COSMAC VIP running with a VP551 board.
</p>

<p><strong>vp590.xml</strong></p>
<p>
COSMAC VIP running with a VP590 board.
</p>

<p><strong>vp700-vp590-vp595.xml</strong></p>
<p>
RCA VP700 Tiny BASIC ROM, using the patched <code>vip.32.rom</code> file. In addition, this configuration includes the VP590 and VP595 extension boards.
</p>


<h2>COSMAC VIP II</h2>

<p><strong>ed.xml</strong></p>
<p>
The 'ED' is as built by Ed Keefe and described on his <a href="https://www.cosmacvip.com/VIP2/VIP2.php">COSMAC VIP II</a> page.
</p>

<p>
By default, the COSMAC VIP II 'ED' will start up in Fixed Point Basic (FPB).
</p>

<p>
To start up in ROM Mode:
</p>

<ul>
<li>Press <code>F12</code> (run switch) while pressing <strong>Start</strong></li>
<li>Press <code>C</code> and while keeping it pressed, press <code>F12</code></li>
</ul>
<p>
See the <a href="MainFunctionKeys.htm">Function and Hot Keys</a> section.
</p>

<p>
Memory layout:
</p>

<p><strong>FPB Mode</strong></p>
<pre>
0000-3FFF   FPB ROM
0400-07FF   RAM
0C00-0FFF   RAM
4000-7FFF   RAM
8000        System ROM
</pre>

<p><strong>ROM Mode</strong></p>
<pre>
0000-7FFF   RAM
8000        System ROM
</pre>

<p><strong>rca.xml</strong></p>
<p>
The <strong>RCA</strong> option emulates the RCA version more closely, based on schematics recently found at the Hagley Museum and Library: Sarnoff/RCA Collection - Joseph A. Weisbecker's archived manuscripts and materials.
</p>
<p>
By default, the COSMAC VIP II 'RCA' will start up in Fixed Point Basic (FPB).
</p>

<p><strong>Runtime keys</strong></p>

<p><strong>Windows / Linux</strong></p>
<pre>
Alt+1   Restart in FPB
Alt+2   Restart in RAM
Alt+C   Start VIP Operating System
Alt+3   Halt the VIP II
</pre>

<p><strong>macOS</strong></p>
<pre>
Command+1   Restart in FPB
Command+2   Restart in RAM
Command+C   Start VIP Operating System
Command+3   Halt the VIP II
</pre>

<p>
Memory layout:
</p>
<pre>
0000-7FFF   RAM (size dependent)
8000-BFFF   FPB and VIP System ROM
</pre>


