<h2>VIP2K Membership Card</h2>

<p><strong>monitor-1.3a.xml</strong></p>
<p>
Chuck's VIP2K monitor version 1.3a.
</p>

<p><strong>monitor-1.4,&lt;type&gt;.xml</strong></p>
<p>
Chuck's VIP2K monitor version 1.4 running on NTSC or PAL video.
</p>

<p><strong>monitor-1.5,&lt;type&gt;,chip8.xml</strong></p>
<p>
Chuck's VIP2K monitor version 1.5 running on NTSC or PAL video and Chip-8 ready.
</p>

<p><strong>monitor-1.5,&lt;type&gt;.xml</strong></p>
<p>
Chuck's VIP2K monitor version 1.5 running on NTSC or PAL video.
</p>

<p>
In the default setting, a VT100 terminal is supported, but no VT window will open.
</p>
<p>
The VIP2K does not use terminal I/O except for file transfer functions of the monitor and BASIC. File I/O works even if no video terminal is opened.
</p>
<p>
VIP2K video emulation differs slightly from the real hardware. The top 8 scan lines may not match the original system.
</p>

